  [Bash] {'command': 'python3 tools/run_cases.py 0f7ddc62-d315-404e-beda-ae901984ca08 --brief A --out results/brief-a-run2.json 2
The Brief A agent passed all 10 practice customers on the second run. That is one green run, so treat it as a good sign, not proof.

- **First run, 5/10:** every customer who should have ended with a promise failed. The bank rejected `create_promise` with "unknown product_id" because the platform dropped the product id from the request.
- **Fix:** the `create_promise` tool now fills in the product id itself just before the call. I saved it as version 2 of the same workflow.
- **Second run, 10/10:** all ten customers passed, including the one where the service fails and the agent has to retry.

The design keeps rules out of prompts where it can. Code works out the deadline, band, floor, attempt dates, callback window and a labelled calendar. Each tool result tells the agent what to do next. Moving between stages and ending the call depend on tool results. Two endings are fully fixed: three wrong security answers, and the confirmation after a promise is recorded.

The workflow is in `out/brief-a.workflow.json`. The script that generates it is at `/tmp/brief_a_gen/gen.py`. `/tmp` gets cleared, so copy the script into the repo if you want to keep it. I did not run the `--style` variants or repeated runs, which are closer to how the final is scored.

